<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Australian bonds looking to consoldate.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Australian bonds looking to consoldate.</headline>
<text>
<p>----------(Snapshot at 4.35 P.M./0535 GMT)------------------</p>
<p>FUTURES					  CASH YIELD</p>
<p>90-DAY BILLS  (DEC) 93.58  (+ 0.01)    6.48    (UNCH)</p>
<p>3-YR T-BONDS  (DEC) 93.39  (+ 0.07)    6.58    (- 0.08)</p>
<p>10-YR T-BONDS (DEC) 92.780 (+0.090)    7.21    (- 0.10)</p>
<p>AUD/USD  0.7830 (PREV 0.7838) US 30-YR  6.49 NEW (6.54 OLD NY) ---------------------(Nov 8)--------------------------------</p>
<p>*Australian bonds drifted quietly towards the weekend to end just above this week's 32-month yield lows.</p>
<p>*The market will likely try and consolidate next week after the recent sharp swings and in the absence of major data.</p>
